# Mindmeld Configuration
#
# Most macOS users don't need this file — the defaults below are what the code
# uses when a variable is unset. Copy to .env and uncomment only what you change.
#
# Full reference: README.md (Configuration) and docs/DOCKER.md.

# ============================================
# SOURCE PATHS
# ============================================
# Claude Code is the same path on macOS and Linux.
# CLAUDE_CODE_PATH=~/.claude
#
# Cursor is read under two different names:
#   CURSOR_PATH             — used by the CLI / sync process
#   CURSOR_GLOBALSTATE_PATH — used by docker-compose.local.yml's bind mount
# Linux users need the globalStorage path:
# CURSOR_PATH=~/.config/Cursor/User/globalStorage
# CURSOR_GLOBALSTATE_PATH=~/.config/Cursor/User/globalStorage
#
# If you don't use Cursor, point these at any existing empty directory so the
# Docker bind mount doesn't error.

# ============================================
# DATABASE
# ============================================
# Every machine feeding one shared index must agree on these.
# POSTGRES_HOST=localhost
# POSTGRES_PORT=5433
# POSTGRES_USER=mindmeld
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=mindmeld
# POSTGRES_DB=conversations

# CHROMA_HOST=localhost
# CHROMA_PORT=8001

# Host port published for the mcp container (in-container port is 3000).
# MCP_HTTP_PORT=3847

# ============================================
# OLLAMA
# ============================================
# One Ollama serves both vectorization (bge-m3) and generation (qwen3). The
# default reaches host Ollama via host.docker.internal from containers.
# Change if Ollama is on a different machine:
# OLLAMA_URL=http://192.168.1.100:11434
#
# NOTE: bge-m3 returns ALL-NULL embeddings when Ollama flash attention is ON.
# Whatever instance OLLAMA_URL points at must have it off. Verify before
# trusting a new endpoint — expect a long, non-null array:
#   curl -s localhost:11434/api/embed -d '{"model":"bge-m3","input":"probe"}' | head -c 80
#
# Max requests in flight. When Ollama is reached over an SSH tunnel, concurrent
# requests saturate the tunnel and each balloons to ~30s — the tunnel, not the
# GPU, is the bottleneck. Raise this only when Ollama is local.
# OLLAMA_MAX_CONCURRENCY=1
# OLLAMA_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
# OLLAMA_MAX_RETRIES=3
# OLLAMA_RETRY_DELAY_MS=5000

# ============================================
# MODELS
# ============================================
# Changing EMBEDDING_MODEL invalidates every existing vector — you must re-embed.
# EMBEDDING_MODEL=bge-m3
# EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS=1024
# EMBEDDING_BATCH_SIZE=100
# SUMMARIZE_MODEL=qwen3:8b

# ============================================
# JOB CADENCE (seconds)
# ============================================
# SYNC_INTERVAL_SECONDS=3600       # host sync loop (scripts/sync-host.sh)
# CENTROID_INTERVAL_SECONDS=25200  # mindmeld-centroids, 7 hours
# WARMUP_INTERVAL_SECONDS=21600    # mindmeld-warmups, 6 hours

# ============================================
# CLOUDFLARE TUNNEL (optional)
# ============================================
# Mindmeld has no authentication of its own — the tunnel is the access control.
#   docker compose --profile tunnel up -d
# CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=your-tunnel-token
